title: CLI configuration
tags: Configuration
kind: reference
summary: cli/config.toml — the daemon port, the page size, a default repository and the tag field names; flags and variables win.

`~/.config/metafolder/cli/config.toml`. A missing or malformed file, or a missing key,
stops `mf` with exit code 2, before any daemon call ([[No runtime fallback]]); only
`[repo]` may be left out. `mf --config FILE` reads that file instead, so a script is
immune to your personal settings.

|!Table |!Key |!Shipped value |!For |
|`[settings]` |`daemon-port` |`7523` |used when neither `-p`/`--port` nor `METAFOLDER_DAEMON_PORT` is given |
| |`page-size` |`500` |the page size `mf` asks for while streaming a listing |
| |`reconcile-poll-interval-ms` |`200` |how often `mf reconcile` polls its task, when `--poll-interval` is not given |
|`[repo]` |`name` or `uuid` |— |a default repository, used when no `-n`/`-u` (nor their variables) is given; without one, a command needing a repository and given none is a usage error |
|`[tag]` |`type-field`, `entry-type`, `path-field`, `positive`, `negative`, `mixed`, `always`, `partition`, `sparse` |`mf_schema`, `tag`, `path`, `tag`, `negative_tag`, `mixed_tag`, `always`, `partition`, `sparse` |the field names of the tag model `mf tag` works with (the GUI's tagging scripts use the same): [[Tag entries and references]] |

Precedence, for every setting: an explicit flag or environment variable, then the
file.
